sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Good day!\r\nHere is an simplified version of my model:\r\n```python\r\nclass A(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'a'\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    deleted_when = Column(DateTime, server_default=None, default=None)\r\n\r\nclass B(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = 'b'\r\n    id = Column(Integer, primary_key=True)\r\n    a_id = Column(Integer, ForeignKey(A.id))\r\n    a = relationship(\r\n        A,\r\n        primaryjoin=\"and_(A.id==B.a_id, \"\r\n                    \"A.deleted_when == None)\")\r\n```\r\nand here is a snippet of code:\r\n```python\r\na = A()\r\n# OR take an existing a=db.query(A).first() with empty deleted_when\r\ndb.query(B).filter_by(a=a).all()\r\n```\r\nThis worked fine in 1.2.x, but now crashes in 1.3.3\r\nBasically I'm running in this exception:\r\nhttps://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/blob/b26642e2364836fe9a8ee25c1cf4551901ce0c37/lib/sqlalchemy/orm/relationships.py#L1584\r\n\r\nI think that, when the column has a default or server_default, that value should be returned instead of `NEVER_SET`.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users